# Format: concept | intent | answer | keywords | patterns | tl | bis
# 4 entries, one genuinely distinct fact per line.
kumusta | definition | Kumusta is the Filipino greeting, and the same word means how are things and what is up, so a single word covers both the greeting and the question behind it. The full question is kumusta ka, and the answer is usually kumusta rin or maganda, and the word also works with a plural subject. It is the greeting people use all day rather than only on arrival, so saying it when you already know someone is a way of checking in rather than of meeting. The other common greeting is magandang araw, literally a good day, which is more a remark about the weather than a question, and the two are frequently used together. Learners often try to say good morning in Filipino as a literal translation, which produces something a Filipino understands but would not use, since the time of day is normally covered by the separate greeting magandang umaga or magandang hapon. | how are you, greeting, kumusta ka, maganda, hi, check in | anong meaning ng kumusta, kumusta meaning, how do you say hello in filipino | kumusta | kumusta
